I see the full picture. In the gh-865 live scenario: head carries in_progress check-runs with run ids on a completed kicker run. `classify()` would mark them 'run-concluded' zombies (past 5-min grace). So `gGreenZombies.zombies.length > 0` → the green cover is VOID → falls through to the dispatch gate → placeholder gate at 2333. There `vPh` = [] (all have run ids) → conclude step skipped entirely → falls to normal dispatch (re-dispatch same sha) which is AC3 legacy remedy for run-id ghosts... but per the ticket, re-dispatch doesn't cure these: these are required contexts evaluated from the kicker suite's check-runs; a same-sha re-dispatch mints new runs but GitHub's required-context evaluation takes LATEST per (context, head) — a new dispatched validation run would stamp 'Quality gate' etc. Actually in the live case there were already 4 green CI runs and SM success stamps on the same head, yet still BLOCKED — because the in_progress placeholders were newer (18:51) than the green stamps (19:04? hmm). Whatever — ticket says conclude them in place.

Now the fix design (minimal, generalized):

In checkRunZombies.js add:

```js
/**
 * Orphaned run-linked checks (gh-865) — the numeric-id twin of the
 * placeholder. Live fa #1457 (head fd1b9aa2): GitHub minted in_progress
 * placeholder check-runs WITH numeric run ids on the kicker suite after
 * the ~10-13 min speculative window expired; the owning kicker run
 * (38164305157) concluded success, nothing will ever conclude the checks.
 * gh-852's detector keys on the MISSING run id, so it missed them.
 *
 * Generalized orphan rule: a PENDING check-run whose OWNING RUN has
 * CONCLUSIONED (any conclusion, past the propagation grace) is
 * definitionally orphaned — conclude it with the mirrored verdict. The
 * call site keeps the gh-857 fail-safes (no conclusion without a real
 * green verdict on the head; never while a live run covers the head).
 */
function orphanedRunChecks(checkRuns, resolveRun, nowMs, opts) {
    var out = [];
    var graceMs = _num(opts, 'runConcludedGraceMinutes', DEFAULT_RUN_CONCLUDED_GRACE_MINUTES) * 60 * 1000;
    var now = typeof nowMs === 'number' ? nowMs : Date.now();
    (checkRuns || []).forEach(function (cr) {
        if (!isPendingCheckRun(cr)) return;
        var runId = runIdOf(cr);
        if (runId === null || typeof resolveRun !== 'function') return;
        var state;
        try { state = resolveRun(runId); } catch (e) { return; } // fail safe — retry next tick
        if (state === null || state === undefined) return;      // no-run variant keeps the legacy remedy
        if (String(state.status || '').toLowerCase() !== 'completed') return; // live (or odd) — untouched
        var endTs = Date.parse(state.updated_at || state.created_at || '');
        var lag = isNaN(endTs) ? null : now - endTs;
        if (lag !== null && lag >= 0 && lag <= graceMs) return;  // propagation lag
        out.push({ name: (cr && cr.name) || null, runId: runId,
                   id: (cr && cr.id !== undefined && cr.id !== null) ? cr.id : null,
                   reason: 'orphan-run-concluded' });
    });
    return out;
}
```

Wait — subtle: classify() 'run-concluded' requires `concl` non-null; completed without conclusion → fail safe live. I keep that: only conclude when the owning run has any conclusion? My version above treats completed (any conclusion incl. cancelled) past grace as orphan. The ticket says "(any conclusion)". For cancelled owning runs — classify already zombie-pushes those with reason 'cancelled' and the re-dispatch remedy exists. Concluding a check whose owning run was cancelled, with a mirrored GREEN verdict from the head's green cover... Hmm — is that safe? The check-run's own run was cancelled, but the head carries a real completed-success dispatched validation run (greenCoverRun). The orphan rule per ticket: "an in_progress check-run whose OWNING RUN has concluded (any conclusion) is definitionally orphaned → conclude it with the mirrored verdict". The mirrored verdict comes from the green cover (AC3, never conclude without a real green verdict). If the head has no green cover, no conclusion. I think including cancelled is per-spec ("any conclusion"). But minimal + safe: I'll include any completed owning run past grace, mirroring classify's shape but without requiring non-cancelled. Actually wait — should I require conclusion non-null? state.completed without conclusion is odd; classify fails safe to live. I'll fail safe likewise (require a conclusion? no — "any conclusion" implies a conclusion exists). Let me require `concl` truthy, mirroring classify, except cancelled is INCLUDED here (unlike classify which also pushes cancelled as zombie). Simplest correct per ticket: completed + conclusion present (any) + past grace → orphan.

Hmm, but hold on: cancelled owning runs — the ghost might legitimately be... no; the run is over, nothing will conclude the check. The mirror verdict requirement keeps it honest. OK include.

